        <mxCell id="x_5deawCPJIRI2wgEKRB-43" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=20;" value="Flow and Connections&#xa;1. User Access Flow   - User opens the Netflix application. &#xa;The client sends a request to the DNS. &#xa;DNS resolves the request and directs the user to the appropriate region/service. &#xa;The request reaches the Load Balancer/API Gateway.&#xa;The API Gateway authenticates the request and routes it to the required backend service.&#xa;2. Login / Authentication Flow   User → API Gateway → Authentication/User Service → Database   - User submits login credentials.   - Authentication service verifies the credentials.   - User session/token is created.   - Authentication information is returned to the client.3. Content Browsing Flow   User → API Gateway → Content Service → Cache/Database   - User requests the home page or content information.   - Content Service checks the cache for frequently accessed information.   - If data is not available in the cache, it is retrieved from the database.   - The response is returned to the user.&#xa;4. Search Flow   User → API Gateway → Search Service → Search Index   - User enters a search query.   - API Gateway forwards the request to the Search Service.   - Search Service queries the search index.   - Matching movies/shows are returned to the client.&#xa;5. Recommendation Flow   User → API Gateway → Recommendation Service   - User requests personalized recommendations.   - Recommendation Service uses user preferences, viewing history, ratings,     and other behavioral data.   - Recommendations are returned to the client.&#xa;6. Video Streaming Flow   User → API Gateway → Streaming Service                         ↓                    Authorization                         ↓                       CDN                         ↓                  Object Storage   - User selects a movie or TV show.   - The client requests playback authorization/metadata from the backend.   - Streaming Service verifies that the user has access to the content.   - The client receives the required manifest/playback information.   - The client requests video segments from the CDN.   - CDN serves the video segments from the nearest edge location.   - If the required content is not present at the CDN edge, it is fetched     from origin/object storage and cached at the CDN.   - Video is delivered directly from the CDN to the user.&#xa;7. Adaptive Streaming Flow   User ↔ CDN   - Video is stored in multiple resolutions/bitrates.   - The client monitors network speed and device capabilities.   - The client requests an appropriate video segment quality.   - Quality can automatically increase or decrease depending on network conditions.&#xa;8. Viewing Activity Flow   User → API Gateway → Playback/Activity Service → Message Queue                                                  ↓                                             Data Processing                                                  ↓                                      Analytics/Recommendation   - Playback events such as play, pause, completion, and watch duration     are generated.   - Events are sent asynchronously through a message queue/event streaming system.   - Data processing systems consume these events.   - Processed data is used for analytics and improving recommendations.&#xa;9. Watchlist / Viewing History Flow   User → API Gateway → User/History Service → Cache/Database   - User adds or removes content from the watchlist.   - Viewing progress and history are updated.   - Frequently accessed information can be cached.   - Persistent data is stored in the database.&#xa;10. Subscription &amp; Payment Flow    User → API Gateway → Subscription Service → Payment Service                                             ↓                                          Database    - User selects a subscription plan.    - Subscription Service sends the payment request to the Payment Service.    - Payment is processed through an external payment provider.    - Subscription status is updated after successful payment.    - The user&#39;s access rights are updated accordingly.&#xa;11. Failure Handling    - Load Balancers distribute traffic across multiple instances.    - Services are replicated across multiple servers/availability zones.    - CDN provides geographically distributed content delivery.    - Databases use replication and backups for durability.    - Failed service instances can be replaced automatically." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="610" width="560" x="280" y="4660" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
